cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "P1F-Census: perfect one-factorizations of K14-K20 with non-trivial automorphisms"
message: >-
  This repository holds the search engine and the run scripts. If you use a
  CATALOGUE, cite the Zenodo dataset DOI for the graph in question rather than
  this repository -- record numbers are positions within a published version,
  and only the dataset DOIs pin them. The four datasets are listed under
  identifiers below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ivanov
    given-names: Andrei V.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1574-6716"
  - family-names: Tertitski
    given-names: Leonid M.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-7556-9552"
repository-code: "https://github.com/LeAndr-Graph/P1F-Census"
license: MIT
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22238984
    description: "K18, |Aut| > 1 -- complete catalogue (10,710 classes)"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22215011
    description: "K20, |Aut| > 3 -- complete catalogue (230 classes)"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22880728
    description: "K20, |Aut| = 3 -- complete catalogue (149,606 classes)"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22548329
    description: "K17,17 perfect 1-factorizations, from the K18 catalogue (104,088 classes)"
keywords:
  - perfect one-factorization
  - one-factorization
  - complete graph
  - automorphism group
  - exhaustive classification
  - combinatorial design
  - Latin square
